From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luca Kasper <luca.kasper@technative.eu>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dwrite: Avoid NULL dereference in create_matching_font on a
 null font collection.

layout_run_get_last_resort_font() passes range->collection straight through,
and that pointer is NULL for a range that never had a collection assigned.
create_matching_font() then calls IDWriteFontCollection_FindFamilyName() on
it, which dereferences the COM vtable at offset 0 and raises an access
violation.

Under Wine the exception surfaces through user_callback_handler, which logs
"ignoring exception c0000005" and unwinds without releasing the critical
section the faulting thread held. Every other thread then blocks on that
section forever, so the application deadlocks rather than crashing outright.
Photoshop 2021 hits this when opening its New Document dialog: the dialog
never appears and the UI stops responding.

The caller already handles failure here by retrying against the system
collection with Tahoma, so returning E_FAIL is enough to reach that path and
render the dialog.

Written against Wine 11.12. PhialsBasement/wine-adobe-installers carried an
equivalent fix as a binary trampoline patched into dwrite.dll; this is the
same change made in source so it survives a Wine version bump.
---
 dlls/dwrite/analyzer.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/dwrite/analyzer.c b/dlls/dwrite/analyzer.c
--- a/dlls/dwrite/analyzer.c
+++ b/dlls/dwrite/analyzer.c
@@ -2594,6 +2594,9 @@ HRESULT create_matching_font(IDWriteFontCollection *collection, const WCHAR *name

     *obj = NULL;

+    if (!collection)
+        return E_FAIL;
+
     hr = IDWriteFontCollection_FindFamilyName(collection, name, &i, &exists);
     if (FAILED(hr))
         return hr;
--
2.51.0

